I have a problem running nethack on my 386/40 (no 80387).

The version is:

PC NetHack Version 3.1.3 - last build Mon Jul 19 18:51:27 1993.

I obtained it from the main FTP site stated in the FAQ.

When I attempt to run Nethack under Desqview on this machine,
I get the following error message:

General Protection Fault at eip=c2204
Call frame traceback EIPs:
  0x000c2204
  0x000b5688
  0x000b4050
  0x00043401

Anybody know what this error means?  Nethack runs fine on this machine outside 
of Desqview, and it runs fine on my work machine (a 386/33 WITH a 80387) with
and without Desqview.  Both machines are running:

MSDOS version 6.00
QEMM version  6.04
DESQview version  2.42

Work machine has 8 Megs ram, home machine has only 4 Megs.  
Otherwise the machines have an almost identical configuration. Its
a drag not being able to access the spoiler file when not running under 
Desqview!  I have a 560k window on home machine, so that isn't the
problem.  Home machine is running Doublespace (on a different partition),
but disabeling it made no difference.

Home machine has a Vega motherboard with AMI bios.  It has behaved
strangely before, especially with Desqview X.  It also had problems
with X-window applications generated with the DJGPP compilier, but those
problems appeared to stem from the lack of a coprocessor.  So I 
think the problem is due to some strange incompatability in the Vega
motherboard.  Hopefully someone will prove me wrong!  Work machine
has AMI motherboard (BabyScreamer), it is fine!

